{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice","id":1393566,"title":"Combat Variant-- Players Roll All the Dice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-01T18:53:56-07:00","id":1393566,"title":"Combat Variant-- Players Roll All the Dice","content":"In my never-ending quest to make the game easier to GM, I found myself looking at NPC die pools. I've played around with reducing their size-- from 10d to 4d+3 successes-- but this time I found myself wondering &quot;what if they never roll at all?&quot; The combat system as it currently stands features an awful lot of back-and-forth, with opportunities for the player to interject at every stage. It seems to me that it might be simpler if players did all the rolling. Something like...<ul><li>NPC declares an attack; player rolls Dexterity + (Dodge/Melee/whatever) against their attack DC. Effects that would boost defense by a flat +1 instead grant one auto-success on this roll. If she succeeds, she avoids the blow.<ul><li>If the withering attack hits, the player rolls dice equal to her soak, minus one die per threshold failures on the previous roll, against the NPC's damage DC. She loses one Ini per threshold failure on this roll, to a minimum of the attacker's Overwhelm.</li> <li>If the decisive attack hits, the player takes one level of damage per three Initiative the attacker had accumulated, rounding up. (Unless Hardness would block the attack)</li> </ul></li> <li>For things like Rush and Disengage, the player would roll their pool against the NPC's combat movement DC.</li> </ul><br /> And... that's pretty much it. Players attacking NPCs would work normally. (Or you could have the players roll damage + threshold successes, subtract half the NPC's Soak, and that's the Ini damage). My feeling is that re-framing attacks this way would help new players remember when they can use Charms, simplify the back-and-forth involved in Soak, make it easier to coach new players through their turn, and just... overall feel smoother and more under the player's control. The main complication I can think of is dice trick Charms like Hail-Shattering Practice that depend on the foe's roll, but you <i>should </i>be able to apply them to your own Parry roll with no ill effect, I think?<br /> <br /> Anyway. Thoughts? Issues? Opinions? Angry shouting?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T19:35:55-07:00","id":1393568,"title":"","content":"The soak part kind of makes my head spin, but everything else seems straightforward. The dice tricks can apply to the parry roll, but they'll also have their math off a bit. Like for example a monster may have double 9s on its attack roll, and that won't translate to the parry roll exactly, although getting rid of the double 10s would be almost the same.<br /> <br /> You'll have to figure out how to deal with clashes though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T20:13:21-07:00","id":1393573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393568#post1393568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The soak part kind of makes my head spin, but everything else seems straightforward. The dice tricks can apply to the parry roll, but they'll also have their math off a bit. Like for example a monster may have double 9s on its attack roll, and that won't translate to the parry roll exactly, although getting rid of the double 10s would be almost the same.<br /> <br /> You'll have to figure out how to deal with clashes though.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the soak:<br /> <br /> Let's say that Three Silk Stars is fighting a Blood Ape.<ul><li>She has Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Melee 4 and is wearing light armor for a final soak of 6.</li> <li>The Blood Ape's die pools, converted to static DCs, would be Attack (Claw) 6 and Damage (Claw) 8</li> </ul><br /> The ape attacks. Silk rolls 9 dice to parry (Dex+Melee) and gets 4 successes. Compared to the ape's attack DC of 6, that's two failures, meaning she just got hit soundly. To determine how much withering damage she takes, she rolls (6 base soak - 2 threshold failures)=4 dice for soak. She gets 3 successes, not nearly enough-- she missed the damage DC by 5, meaning she takes 5 points of withering damage.<br /> <br /> Does that make more sense?<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> NPC charms can be tweaked to either work based on the player's roll (instead of double 9s, maybe the player's 7s count as failures-- that works out the same, I think), or just by flat bonuses. I'm inclined towards the latter-- the aforementioned Blood Ape's Rending Claw Slash can become &quot;+2 to the attack's damage DC, +3 if the target rolls 6 or more failures on their defense roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Clashes shouldn't really need anything? The player rolls an attack against the NPC's attack DC; if she wins, she lands a hit and gets the extra damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T20:24:33-07:00","id":1393575,"title":"","content":"Yeah that should be okay. Also how would onslaught penalties work? Just subtract successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T23:35:17-07:00","id":1393584,"title":"","content":"The idea seems clever. I get how it helps lighten the work of the GM, but I'm unsure putting all the maths on the shoulders of the players in a game heavy like Exalted will actually result in something smoother. I'm curious to hear your feedback though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T06:08:16-07:00","id":1393611,"title":"","content":"Soak might need some calibration - overwhelming damage successes is twice as much as overwhelming damage dice.<br /> Additionally, there are effects that trigger off of taking 0 damage - Essence Gathering Temper, Hardened Shell Superiority, Blithe Unruffled Plumage<br /> None of these seem insurmountable though.<br /> <br /> Overall it seems like a reasonable alteration to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T06:48:40-07:00","id":1393619,"title":"","content":"As a general RPG system mechanic? Love it!<br /> <br /> As an Exalted hack? Meh.<br /> <br /> Seems like a lot of conversion work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T06:58:19-07:00","id":1393621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393575#post1393575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that should be okay. Also how would onslaught penalties work? Just subtract successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Though I might turn them into die penalties as a low-key way to make being outnumbered less lethal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393584#post1393584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea seems clever. I get how it helps lighten the work of the GM, but I'm unsure putting all the maths on the shoulders of the players in a game heavy like Exalted will actually result in something smoother. I'm curious to hear your feedback though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it actually increases the math load, though. From what I've seen, the things that slow down combat are:<ul><li>The repeated back-and-forth necessary to add threshold successes and subtract soak from the withering damage roll</li> <li>Deciding which Charms to use and figuring out their combined effects</li> <li>Physically rolling and counting large numbers of dice.</li> </ul><br /> If you use soak-as-successes for NPCs, this revision should help with all of that.<ul><li>Less back and forth-- Instead of &quot;He attacks, you using any defensive Charms? Okay, he rolls 7, what's your parry up to? Then he hits you by 3, what's your Soak? Any more Charms? Okay, that's... 12 base damage, minus eight, plus three... okay, 7 dice &lt;rolls&gt;&quot;, The exchange becomes &quot;roll parry. No? Roll soak minus three.&quot;</li> <li>Charms should be easier, because they're more consistent-- when you roll, you can modify it with Charms. Better yet, you don't have to repeatedly stop and check for Charms mid-action.</li> <li>Rolling... won't really be any faster, but it'll at least be the player doing it-- they don't have to sit and wait for me to count dice, and it's not going to cost me any of my brain-space.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393611#post1393611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soak might need some calibration - overwhelming damage successes is twice as much as overwhelming damage dice.<br /> Additionally, there are effects that trigger off of taking 0 damage - Essence Gathering Temper, Hardened Shell Superiority, Blithe Unruffled Plumage<br /> None of these seem insurmountable though.<br /> <br /> Overall it seems like a reasonable alteration to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, true. I've used the &quot;overwhelm as minimum damage&quot; thing before, and I don't mind it-- it means more Initiative is flowing around the battlefield and everything's more fluid-- but admittedly no-one had a charm like Essence Gathering Temper. Easy enough to modify those when they come up, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T08:46:59-07:00","id":1393645,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't think this would take too much conversion work as some others may think, but the reason 1e moved away from contested rolls was speed. Part of the problem in that is that battle lasted a long time until one side got really unlucky. My worry is that in 3e, which combat takes longer than the past editions on average, will really compound this with withering and decisive.<br /> <br /> Aside from making the resolution slower (more rolls) you also run into the problem of damage. Soak in Exalted has always been an issue. One can trivially outpace the damage one can belt out with soak in all but the most extreme cases (EX: Rampage Berserker Attack). This isn't the case in some issues, such as DnD where 99.9% of the time how well you hit is irrelevant outside of crits. Even in 2d20, a success based system, the *vast* majority of your damage comes from your base damage + attribute.<br /> <br /> So while you can do this, it would involve some final eyeballing of the math to get things right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T01:06:15-07:00","id":1393752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393621#post1393621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Though I might turn them into die penalties as a low-key way to make being outnumbered less lethal.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think it actually increases the math load, though. From what I've seen, the things that slow down combat are:<ul><li>The repeated back-and-forth necessary to add threshold successes and subtract soak from the withering damage roll</li> <li>Deciding which Charms to use and figuring out their combined effects</li> <li>Physically rolling and counting large numbers of dice.</li> </ul><br /> If you use soak-as-successes for NPCs, this revision should help with all of that.<ul><li>Less back and forth-- Instead of &quot;He attacks, you using any defensive Charms? Okay, he rolls 7, what's your parry up to? Then he hits you by 3, what's your Soak? Any more Charms? Okay, that's... 12 base damage, minus eight, plus three... okay, 7 dice &lt;rolls&gt;&quot;, The exchange becomes &quot;roll parry. No? Roll soak minus three.&quot;</li> <li>Charms should be easier, because they're more consistent-- when you roll, you can modify it with Charms. Better yet, you don't have to repeatedly stop and check for Charms mid-action.</li> <li>Rolling... won't really be any faster, but it'll at least be the player doing it-- they don't have to sit and wait for me to count dice, and it's not going to cost me any of my brain-space.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Eh, true. I've used the &quot;overwhelm as minimum damage&quot; thing before, and I don't mind it-- it means more Initiative is flowing around the battlefield and everything's more fluid-- but admittedly no-one had a charm like Essence Gathering Temper. Easy enough to modify those when they come up, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah ok I suppose I'm pretty convinced it could work. How do you figure out Damage DC of NPCs ? I guess I have a pretty solid idea about the Attack DC (just take the average of their attack), but I'm not sure about the Damage DC ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:00:32-07:00","id":1393765,"title":"","content":"Sandact6-- I'm not putting in more opposed rolls, just shuffling around which values are static and which are rolled. RAW the NPC attacker rolls attack and damage against the PC's static defense and soak; by these rules the PC rolls defense and soak against the NPC's static attack and damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393752#post1393752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah ok I suppose I'm pretty convinced it could work. How do you figure out Damage DC of NPCs ? I guess I have a pretty solid idea about the Attack DC (just take the average of their attack), but I'm not sure about the Damage DC ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as any other way you convert a die pool to a static value-- divide by two and round up. (You would admittedly have to rejigger their Charms a bit.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:13:51-07:00","id":1393766,"title":"","content":"3e has already moved away from PC/NPC rules symmetry more than previous editions with QCs, so I think something like this is a natural step further if you're into it. Treating the NPCs exactly like PCs (except run by the ST) is a convenience for the writer as much as anything, so they don't need two sets of mechanics. But if you're willing to put in the work there's no particular reason not to just turn NPCs into sets of static values and put all the randomness on the players.<br /> <br /> 4e D&amp;D embraced this asymmetry idea in a BIG way, and I think it was a strength in that sysyem (there were things I didn't like about that edition, but this wasn't really one of them). Fair warning though, the further you go down that path, the harder it is to do PVP effectively. Also it might require some extra suspension of disbelief in a world like Exalted where your most potent opponenrs are other Exalted and so, presumably, are more like yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:46:12-07:00","id":1393771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393766#post1393766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e has already moved away from PC/NPC rules symmetry more than previous editions with QCs, so I think something like this is a natural step further if you're into it. Treating the NPCs exactly like PCs (except run by the ST) is a convenience for the writer as much as anything, so they don't need two sets of mechanics. But if you're willing to put in the work there's no particular reason not to just turn NPCs into sets of static values and put all the randomness on the players.<br /> <br /> 4e D&amp;D embraced this asymmetry idea in a BIG way, and I think it was a strength in that sysyem (there were things I didn't like about that edition, but this wasn't really one of them). Fair warning though, the further you go down that path, the harder it is to do PVP effectively. Also it might require some extra suspension of disbelief in a world like Exalted where your most potent opponenrs are other Exalted and so, presumably, are more like yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I truly believe that crunchy system like Exalted really benefit from asymmetric gameplay. The load on the ST is huge and it's really a core idea to reduce the ST workload. I also think it's way easier to balance the power of players against their environment.<br /> <br /> You are right, however, that it makes interactions with other players more complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T08:44:07-07:00","id":1393784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393766#post1393766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4e D&amp;D embraced this asymmetry idea in a BIG way, and I think it was a strength in that sysyem (there were things I didn't like about that edition, but this wasn't really one of them). Fair warning though, the further you go down that path, the harder it is to do PVP effectively. Also it might require some extra suspension of disbelief in a world like Exalted where your most potent opponenrs are other Exalted and so, presumably, are more like yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed-- 4e had its flaws but I have very fond memory of its monster design and ease of GMing, and abandoning the pretense of symmetry was a big part of that.<br /> <br /> PvP is a potential issue in players-roll-all-the-dice systems, but I don't think it is here-- both characters have all the numbers they need.<ul><li>Alice declares a withering attack against Bob.</li> <li>She rolls (Dex + Melee + Weapon) to hit; he rolls (Dex + Melee) to parry</li> <li>She hits and rolls (Strength + Weapon + Threshold Successes) for damage; he rolls (Soak) and subtracts his successes from hers, and that's how much damage he takes.</li> </ul><br /> <i>NPC vs NPC </i>might be more problematic, but that's rarely worth rolling out at any point. And besides, in Ex3 it takes basically no brainpower to switch between dice pools and averages.<br /> <br /> What I really need to do, I think, is borrow a player or two and roll out a combat using this variant to see how it feels...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T12:47:55-07:00","id":1393825,"title":"","content":"I will give this a try at my game this weekend and report back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:08:05-07:00","id":1393830,"title":"","content":"Rolling defenses opens up the possibility of &quot;botching&quot; your defense, effectively making an enemy's attack unblockable and undodgeable <b>for</b> them. So this will undoubtedly add more RNG to fights and create the possibility for characters to lose fights they would have won for certain with default rules.<br /> <br /> That being said I think it might actually be a good thing since sitting parries of 7/8 are just stupidly powerful in the default rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:10:37-07:00","id":1393832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393825#post1393825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will give this a try at my game this weekend and report back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you!<br /> <br /> I just gave it a try with a player in one-on-one combat, and I think it went pretty well. We were a bit out of practice at Ex3 proper, but the turns went back and forth pretty quickly, and everything felt a lot more... in control, I guess-- the lack of need for &quot;I'm attacking, what's your parry kicked up to?&quot; was really nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T03:58:36-07:00","id":1403641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393619#post1393619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general RPG system mechanic? Love it!<br /> <br /> As an Exalted hack? Meh.<br /> <br /> Seems like a lot of conversion work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not entirely sold on completely reworking Exalted (but if Grod has any write ups to share, I'll happily yoink).<br /> <br /> But I've been looking at Broken Worlds (the Kill Six Billion Demons RPG) and the player not only rolls all the dice, but also takes all the actions. I.e. the PC attacks (or runs away, what-have-you) and if they succeed they wound the enemy, fail and both PC and enemy get wounded or fail and botch just damages the PC.<br /> <br /> Again... not sure if it's worth the effort as an Exalted hack... but it's a really neat system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T06:27:01-07:00","id":1403651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1403641#post1403641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not entirely sold on completely reworking Exalted (but if Grod has any write ups to share, I'll happily yoink).<br /> <br /> But I've been looking at Broken Worlds (the Kill Six Billion Demons RPG) and the player not only rolls all the dice, but also takes all the actions. I.e. the PC attacks (or runs away, what-have-you) and if they succeed they wound the enemy, fail and both PC and enemy get wounded or fail and botch just damages the PC.<br /> <br /> Again... not sure if it's worth the effort as an Exalted hack... but it's a really neat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound interesting. I like that it puts everything down to the decisions of the players. Even more than having the players roll the dice, it captures something from a turn-based game against an AI opponent; you take an action, and then it's immediately your turn again because the AI's response was automatic based on what you did. Circumstances continue to shift and present the player with new options each turn.<br /> <br /> For Exalted... in spirit I think it fits pretty well. The characters are superhuman and go around inflicting their will on the world unless an equal or greater force has other ideas. Mechanical-conversion-wise... I don't know. It seems like the kind of system that amplifies imbalance, and there is lots of inherent imbalance in Exalted. Would need to think about it.<br /> <br /> I think the whole thing would be a *fantastic* fit for shaping combat, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T06:43:54-07:00","id":1403656,"title":"","content":"I am super curious as to how this has worked out for anyone using it. I tend to run *all* the math for my players, and don't mind, since it's faster that way (I'm the only one who reads the books all the way through,) but this sounds like it'd make things even smoother, if it worked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T07:58:45-07:00","id":1403665,"title":"","content":"To me the only real killer for this is that the NPC's are static. I've had some incredible reversal of fortunes for players and NPC's when rolling dice that take the game in entirely unexpected areas. One example was in 2e where a Valor 5 Infernal rolled to see if he'd attack a character. The result was not only a failure but a botch.<br /> <br /> I mean another example is in XCOM, where the RNG can very well make you sweat bullets.<br /> <br /> That said I think it's something easily done and can see how people can have value in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T08:15:24-07:00","id":1403668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1403656#post1403656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am super curious as to how this has worked out for anyone using it. I tend to run *all* the math for my players, and don't mind, since it's faster that way (I'm the only one who reads the books all the way through,) but this sounds like it'd make things even smoother, if it worked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been using these rules exclusively in the campaign I started last month and so far they've worked wonderfully. It really, <i>really </i>makes turns go more smoothly-- so much so that I can't imagine running the system any other way now. Consolidating all of the players' reactions into their own rolls is just... it's tremendous. Seriously, try it and see how much it cuts down the back-and-forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T13:13:47-07:00","id":1410554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393566-combat-variant-players-roll-all-the-dice?p=1393832#post1393832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, thank you!<br /> <br /> I just gave it a try with a player in one-on-one combat, and I think it went pretty well. We were a bit out of practice at Ex3 proper, but the turns went back and forth pretty quickly, and everything felt a lot more... in control, I guess-- the lack of need for &amp;quot;I'm attacking, what's your parry kicked up to?&amp;quot; was really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we used it for a couple weeks before summer kicked in and took a break. It was a bit faster and more efficient. Not &quot;blow your mind&quot; or anything, but my one player was far more engaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}